6.111.m:
Nārada said:
The Kṛṣṇā is Kṛṣṇa's manifest body; the Veṇyā is the god Maheśvara;
not even the four-faced [Brahmā] is competent to describe the efficacy of their confluence.

Nārada said:
Then, hearing that curse, Gāyatrī trembled;
rising up, although restrained by the gods, she cursed Svarā:

The gods said:
O goddess, since all of us, beginning with Brahmā, have now been cursed by you,
if we all turn into inert matter and become rivers here,

They became two gods named Mahābala and Atibalin;
I am not capable, O king, of recounting the glorification of those two rivers.
Brahmā and the other gods went [away], while their streams remain through their portions.

