6.117.m:
Kārtika is the foremost month, ever dear to the Vaiṣṇavas. / A meritorious ocean-going river is rare for those who bathe;

a maiden of noble family and good character is rare; a married couple among men is rare; / a mother is rare in the world, and especially a father;

respect for the virtuous is rare; a righteous son is rare; / residence in Dvārikā is rare; seeing Kṛṣṇa is rare;

bathing in the Gomatī is rare; the Kārtika vow is rare. / Whatever fruit one obtains by giving land to brāhmaṇas during an eclipse of the sun or moon,

that same fruit belongs to one who sleeps on the ground, O child. / One should feed a brāhmaṇa couple and worship them with unguents;

blankets, jewels, and various garments, / and mattresses should be given along with covering sheets;
